# Title: Suspicious Chromium Browser Instance Executed With Custom Extension
# ID: 27ba3207-dd30-4812-abbf-5d20c57d474e
# Status: test
# Level: high
# Author: Aedan Russell, frack113, X__Junior (Nextron Systems)
# Date: 2022-06-19
# Tags: attack.persistence, attack.t1176.001
# Description: Detects a suspicious process spawning a Chromium based browser process with the 'load-extension' flag to start an instance with a custom extension
# Converted by: Sigma Universal SIEM/EDR CLI

index=* eventtype=wineventlog ((parent_process_path="*\\cmd.exe" OR parent_process_path="*\\cscript.exe" OR parent_process_path="*\\mshta.exe" OR parent_process_path="*\\powershell.exe" OR parent_process_path="*\\pwsh.exe" OR parent_process_path="*\\regsvr32.exe" OR parent_process_path="*\\rundll32.exe" OR parent_process_path="*\\wscript.exe") AND (process_path="*\\brave.exe" OR process_path="*\\chrome.exe" OR process_path="*\\msedge.exe" OR process_path="*\\opera.exe" OR process_path="*\\vivaldi.exe") AND process_exec="*--load-extension=*")
